                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "63730473",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197979964791",
                            "num_reviews": 1,
                            "playtime_forever": 129,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 129,
                            "last_played": 1581975503
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Picked up this game and while Tower Defense games aren't a genre I am familiar with, I still had a good time. It's a great game to come back to, a lot of fun playing multiplayer (if you have a friend to play with) and it's clear the developers put a lot of work into it.\n\nI was surprised at how feature complete the game was (it even includes a level editor).\n\nThere's a lot of potential here for the game to grow and I look forward to seeing what they plan on adding to it.\n\nMy only criticisms are minor. The UI for the main menu looks very stock and it's difficult to read some of the smaller text (but I believe there's an option in game to scale this up). Rounds never break, so it's difficult to keep up the pace, but this can be remedied by playing with a friend and splitting your focus between tower building and upgrading.\n\nIf you're a fan of MOBAs and/or Tower Defense game, and are looking for something different, Order of the Gatekeepers is definitely worth checking out.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1582042361,
